# pin: jupyter_server==2.21.1
# upstream: https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1717
#
# Tornado 6.6 deprecated building an HTTPServerRequest from method/uri/version
# and 6.7 (master) requires start_line. jupyter_server's own tests build
# requests the old way, so on master 42 of them fail before they reach the code
# they test -- origin checks, XSRF, static files, websocket pings, the kernel
# connection. Only the tests change; jupyter_server itself is untouched, so a
# Tornado break in jupyter_server's runtime code still shows.
#
# This is the first commit of PR 1717 (2c6cc7e), merged upstream and not yet in
# a release. The PR's other commit is about trash on tmpfs, not Tornado, and
# does not fail here, so it is left out. Delete this file when the pin moves to
# a release that contains the fix; validate_packages.py insists on it.
